# AI implementation

Match **model**, **reasoning effort**, and **prompt depth** to the job. Do not default every OpenAI call to `gpt-5.6-sol`.

Prefer deterministic code for rankings (`apps/scraper/src/tiers/compute.ts`, `@wild-rift-forge/game-data`). Use a model only when the user asks for generated copy or for a judgment the pipeline cannot compute.

## Judgment — trusted player-facing calls

The model **decides** something players will treat as truth:

- Producing or revising a tier list / letter
- Matchup winner, counter strength, draft priority
- Any ranking, score, or “who is better” call not already computed in code

Use `gpt-5.6-sol` with `reasoning_effort: "high"`. Drop to `"medium"` only if batch cost is the constraint — ask first. Give the model the evidence (rates, sample, patch lines, prior letter) and require it to cite those signals. Structured `json_schema` output.

## Everyday — summarize or rewrite

The model **restates** facts the pipeline already computed:

- Tier “why” blurbs (`explain-tiers`)
- Patch lede / watch / movers (`analyze-patch`)
- Titles, tags, one-line copy

Use an everyday chat model (`gpt-4o-mini` unless the job already has a cheaper default). Omit `reasoning_effort` on non-reasoning models; `"low"` only if the model requires the field. One or two sentences. Facts only — do not invent rates or change letters.

`explain-tiers` is everyday copy even though it currently defaults to `gpt-5.6-sol`. Do not raise its effort. When touching that job, keep or move it toward the everyday default; do not treat the current model as the pattern for new summary jobs.

## Mixed jobs

If a request both ranks and explains, **split the calls**: judgment (sol + high) or deterministic compute first, then everyday copy. One expensive call that also writes blurbs is the wrong default.

## Every LLM job

- Structured output (`response_format.json_schema`)
- Prompt: use only supplied facts; never change computed letters or scores
- Env override for the model (`OPENAI_*_MODEL`), default documented in `.env.example`
- Fingerprint prompt + model so reruns skip unchanged rows
- Fail closed on missing `OPENAI_API_KEY` (skip + log, do not crash the scrape)
- Do not raise model or effort “to be safe” on a summary job
